{"id":"p10-l08","minutes":35,"summary":"A hardware timer turns a fast clock into a precise slow one by counting, and two registers set the rate. You derive f_update = f_clk/((PSC + 1)(ARR + 1)), work out the best prescaler and reload for any target frequency within 16-bit limits, configure a 1 kHz control tick, and test it with a cycle-level counter model that must hit the frequency within 0.1 %.","html":"<h2 id=\"a-counter-with-two-dividers\">A counter with two dividers</h2>\n<p>An STM32 general-purpose timer is a counter clocked by the timer clock <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (84 MHz for TIM2–TIM7 on an STM32F407 at 168 MHz, from lesson 07). Two registers shape it:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the <strong>prescaler</strong> PSC divides the clock: the counter advances once every <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">PSC</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> clock cycles;</li>\n<li>the <strong>auto-reload</strong> ARR is the top: the counter goes <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span></span></span></span>, then wraps to 0 and raises an <strong>update event</strong> (which can trigger an interrupt, a DMA request or an ADC conversion).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So each update period is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">PSC</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> clock cycles:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">update</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.3074em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3714em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">PSC</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Both are 16-bit on most timers (TIM2 and TIM5 have a 32-bit ARR), so each factor is at most 65 536. The <em>product</em> is fixed by the frequency you want; how you split it is a design choice. A small PSC and a large ARR give the finest resolution for PWM duty or capture timestamps (lessons 11 and 12). A larger PSC gives a slower, human-readable tick, such as 1 µs per count.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"timerpsc\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>The counter rises from 0 to ARR and wraps, firing an update event (dots) on each wrap. Change PSC and ARR: the readout shows the update frequency and its error against the target.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"when-the-division-isn-t-exact\">When the division isn’t exact</h2>\n<p>The product must be an integer, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> rounded. If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> is not an integer, round it and accept a frequency error</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ε</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.3991em;vertical-align:-0.9721em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9721em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">65</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">536</span></span></span></span>, it must be factored into two 16-bit factors, and a prime-ish <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> may need a small compromise. Searching every PSC from 0 to 65 535 with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ARR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">round</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">PSC</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> finds the best split in a fraction of a millisecond on a host.</p>\n<p>Note the shadow registers: writes to PSC and ARR take effect at the next update event (ARR only if ARPE is set), so set <code>EGR.UG = 1</code> once after configuration to load them immediately.</p>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A 1 kHz control tick from 84 MHz.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">84</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000/1000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">84</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span></span></span></span>, too big for one 16-bit register.</li>\n<li>PSC = 83 makes a 1 MHz counter (1 µs per count), and ARR = 999 makes 1000 counts: exact.</li>\n<li>A 44.1 kHz audio rate: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">84</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000/44</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1904.76</span></span></span></span>, so PSC = 0, ARR = 1904 gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">84</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000/1905</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">44</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">094.5</span></span></span></span> Hz, an error of −0.012 %.</li>\n<li>A 1 Hz tick: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">84</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span></span></span></span> needs PSC + 1 ≥ 84 000 000 / 65 536 ≈ 1282. The smallest divisor of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> above that is 1344, so PSC = 1343, ARR = 62 499 (1344 × 62 500), exact.</li>\n<li>The search’s own 1 kHz answer is PSC = 1, ARR = 41 999: the same product, 84 000, split for the finest resolution. PSC = 83, ARR = 999 is the readable 1 µs-per-count choice; both are exact.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">timer_config.c</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-c\"><span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">include</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&lt;math.h&gt;</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">typedef</span> <span class=\"hljs-class\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">struct</span> {</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> psc, arr; <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> f, err; } tim_cfg;\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* best (PSC, ARR) for a target update rate; 16-bit fields; ties prefer the largest ARR (finest resolution) */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> tim_cfg <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">tim_search</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fclk, <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> target)</span> {\n  tim_cfg best = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e9</span>};\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> psc = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; psc &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">65535</span>; psc++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> arr1 = round(fclk / target / (psc + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>));\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (arr1 &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> || arr1 &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">65536</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">continue</span>;\n    <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> f = fclk / ((psc + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * arr1), err = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(f - target) / target;\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (err &lt; best.err - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>) best = (tim_cfg){psc, (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span>)arr1 - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, f, err};\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> best;\n}\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* register-level model: count timer-clock cycles, fire an update when CNT wraps from ARR */</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">static</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">count_updates</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> psc, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> arr, <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> clk_cycles)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint32_t</span> pre = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, cnt = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> updates = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> c = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; c &lt; clk_cycles; c++) {\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (pre == psc) { pre = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (cnt == arr) { cnt = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; updates++; } <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> cnt++; } <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> pre++;\n  }\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> updates;\n}\n<span class=\"hljs-meta\">#<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">define</span> CHECK(c) do { <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (!(c)) { printf(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;FAIL line %d: %s\\n&quot;</span>, __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">main</span><span class=\"hljs-params\">(<span class=\"hljs-type\">void</span>)</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> fclk = <span class=\"hljs-number\">84e6</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">const</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span> targets[] = {<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">44100</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20000</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3333</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>};\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> (<span class=\"hljs-type\">int</span> i = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>; i++) {\n    tim_cfg c = tim_search(fclk, targets[i]);\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;%8.0f Hz: PSC=%5u ARR=%5u -&gt; %.4f Hz (%.4f %%)\\n&quot;</span>, targets[i], c.psc, c.arr, c.f, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * c.err);\n    CHECK(c.psc &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">65535</span> &amp;&amp; c.arr &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">65535</span>);\n    CHECK(c.err &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.001</span>);                                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* within 0.1 % */</span>\n  }\n  tim_cfg t = tim_search(fclk, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>);\n  CHECK((t.psc + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * (t.arr + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">84000</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* the 1 kHz tick from the worked example, checked against the cycle-level model over 0.25 s */</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> n = count_updates(<span class=\"hljs-number\">83</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">999</span>, (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span>)(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.25</span> * fclk));\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PSC=83 ARR=999: %llu updates in 0.25 s\\n&quot;</span>, (<span class=\"hljs-type\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">long</span> <span class=\"hljs-type\">long</span>)n);\n  CHECK(n == <span class=\"hljs-number\">250</span>);\n  tim_cfg a = tim_search(fclk, <span class=\"hljs-number\">44100</span>);\n  CHECK(a.psc == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> &amp;&amp; a.arr == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1904</span> &amp;&amp; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>(a.f - <span class=\"hljs-number\">44094.488</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span> na = count_updates(a.psc, a.arr, (<span class=\"hljs-type\">uint64_t</span>)fclk / <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>);   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">/* 0.1 s */</span>\n  CHECK(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">fabs</span>((<span class=\"hljs-type\">double</span>)na / <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">44100</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">44100</span> &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.001</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">printf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS\\n&quot;</span>);\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>;\n}</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>You need a 1 µs timestamp counter that wraps as rarely as possible on a 16-bit timer at 84 MHz. What PSC and ARR, and how often does it wrap?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>PSC = 83 makes 1 MHz; ARR = 65 535 (the maximum) wraps every 65.536 ms. For longer intervals, count the update events in software (an overflow counter) or use the 32-bit TIM2, which wraps every 71.6 minutes at 1 MHz.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>You want 20 kHz PWM with the finest duty resolution at 84 MHz. What split, and how many duty steps?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4200</span></span></span></span>. PSC = 0, ARR = 4199 gives 4200 duty steps (about 12 bits). Any larger PSC divides the resolution by PSC + 1 for no benefit.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p10-l08\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"a-counter-with-two-dividers","title":"A counter with two dividers"},{"id":"when-the-division-isn-t-exact","title":"When the division isn’t exact"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p10-l08-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>f_clk = 84 MHz, PSC = 83, ARR = 999. Update frequency in Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>84 MHz / 84 000.</p>\n","answer":1000,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p10-l08-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>With PSC = 0, ARR = 1904 at 84 MHz, the update rate in Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K rounded to 1905.</p>\n","answer":44094.49,"tol":0.0001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p10-l08-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Frequency error of that setting against 44.1 kHz, in percent?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Small, and fine for most uses.</p>\n","answer":-0.0125,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p10-l08-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>How long between wraps of a 16-bit counter at 1 MHz, in ms?</p>\n","explain":"<p>65 536 counts of 1 µs.</p>\n","answer":65.536,"tol":0.001,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p10-l08-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why prefer PSC = 0, ARR = 4199 over PSC = 3, ARR = 1049 for 20 kHz PWM?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The ARR range is the number of duty steps.</p>\n","options":["lower power","it avoids shadow registers","higher update frequency","four times the duty-cycle resolution"],"answer":3},{"id":"p10-l08-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>You wrote new PSC and ARR values but the old rate continues until the next wrap. Why?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Shadow registers.</p>\n","options":["PSC (and ARR with ARPE) are buffered until an update event; set EGR.UG to load now","the counter is 32-bit","the values are too small","the timer clock is off"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"timer_config.c","lang":"c","src":"#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\ntypedef struct { uint32_t psc, arr; double f, err; } tim_cfg;\n\n/* best (PSC, ARR) for a target update rate; 16-bit fields; ties prefer the largest ARR (finest resolution) */\nstatic tim_cfg tim_search(double fclk, double target) {\n  tim_cfg best = {0, 0, 0, 1e9};\n  for (uint32_t psc = 0; psc <= 65535; psc++) {\n    double arr1 = round(fclk / target / (psc + 1));\n    if (arr1 < 1 || arr1 > 65536) continue;\n    double f = fclk / ((psc + 1) * arr1), err = fabs(f - target) / target;\n    if (err < best.err - 1e-12) best = (tim_cfg){psc, (uint32_t)arr1 - 1, f, err};\n  }\n  return best;\n}\n\n/* register-level model: count timer-clock cycles, fire an update when CNT wraps from ARR */\nstatic uint64_t count_updates(uint32_t psc, uint32_t arr, uint64_t clk_cycles) {\n  uint32_t pre = 0, cnt = 0; uint64_t updates = 0;\n  for (uint64_t c = 0; c < clk_cycles; c++) {\n    if (pre == psc) { pre = 0; if (cnt == arr) { cnt = 0; updates++; } else cnt++; } else pre++;\n  }\n  return updates;\n}\n#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { printf(\"FAIL line %d: %s\\n\", __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)\n\nint main(void) {\n  const double fclk = 84e6;\n  const double targets[] = {1000, 44100, 1, 20000, 3333, 50};\n  for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n    tim_cfg c = tim_search(fclk, targets[i]);\n    printf(\"%8.0f Hz: PSC=%5u ARR=%5u -> %.4f Hz (%.4f %%)\\n\", targets[i], c.psc, c.arr, c.f, 100 * c.err);\n    CHECK(c.psc <= 65535 && c.arr <= 65535);\n    CHECK(c.err < 0.001);                                    /* within 0.1 % */\n  }\n  tim_cfg t = tim_search(fclk, 1000);\n  CHECK((t.psc + 1) * (t.arr + 1) == 84000);\n  /* the 1 kHz tick from the worked example, checked against the cycle-level model over 0.25 s */\n  uint64_t n = count_updates(83, 999, (uint64_t)(0.25 * fclk));\n  printf(\"PSC=83 ARR=999: %llu updates in 0.25 s\\n\", (unsigned long long)n);\n  CHECK(n == 250);\n  tim_cfg a = tim_search(fclk, 44100);\n  CHECK(a.psc == 0 && a.arr == 1904 && fabs(a.f - 44094.488) < 0.01);\n  uint64_t na = count_updates(a.psc, a.arr, (uint64_t)fclk / 10);   /* 0.1 s */\n  CHECK(fabs((double)na / 0.1 - 44100) / 44100 < 0.001);\n  printf(\"PASS\\n\");\n  return 0;\n}"}]}